Principles of Extractive Metallurgy — Tarun Kumar Kundu, NPTEL (@metal-extract-course: 0, is #reference, #part-of @metal-sources) { r_7VCNEHN5VCQDDQTZ512PSHFZ78
Tarun Kumar Kundu, IIT Kharagpur. Principles of Extractive Metallurgy, NPTEL 113105441. [Official course](https://nptel.ac.in/courses/113105441) · [Full twelve-week syllabus](https://archive.nptel.ac.in/content/syllabus_pdf/113105441.pdf).

Complete the public sequence and worked material. Its unit-process approach connects mineral feeds, fuels/furnaces/refractories, thermal treatment, reduction, sulfide smelting/conversion, refining, hydrometallurgy, electrometallurgy, and environmental systems. Use specific metal cases to test the shared principles rather than learning disconnected industrial names.

Instructor, course identity, complete syllabus, and public layout were checked on 29 October 2026. Preserve the actual run, media/component notices, and later revisions; free lectures do not establish a blanket redistribution licence or access to every campus assessment. Exam registration and certification are separate from the learning work. All course media remain external.

